-- title:
--   Valuative cover of the blown-up supersingular chart by B and its ends
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $q$ and $\ell$ are primes, $M'$ is a non-zero natural number with $q \nmid M'$, and $\ell$ satisfies $\ell \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ and $\ell \mid M'$. The field $L$ has characteristic zero, $\zeta \in L$ is a primitive $q$-th root of unity, and `hι` provides a ring homomorphism $\iota : L \to \mathbb{C}$ with $\iota(\zeta) = e^{2\pi i/q}$. The subgroup $H_1 \le (\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times$ is prescribed by `hH₁` to be the intersection of [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelH q M'`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelJacobian.html#L22), the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/q)^\times$, with the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/\ell)^\times$. The intermediate field $K$ of $L \subseteq L(\!(t)\!)$ is, by `hK`, the $L$-subfield generated by the coefficientwise image in $L(\!(t)\!)$ of the $q$-expansion function field of $\Gamma_{H_1}(q^2M')$ over $\mathbb{Q}$. The ring $A$ is a henselian discrete valuation domain with algebraically closed residue field, an $L$-algebra with $L$ as fraction field, with $q \in \mathfrak{m}_A$ (`hAq`) and $\zeta$ in the image of $A$ (`hζA`), and $K$ is an $A$-algebra compatibly with $L$. The element $j \in K$ is non-zero and, by `hj`, has Laurent expansion the coefficientwise image of the classical series [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157). Further, $\varpi$ generates $\mathfrak{m}_A$ (`hϖ`), and $\varpi_t \in A$ satisfies $\varpi_t^{\,q^2-1} = q\,u$ for some unit $u$ (`hϖt`). Write $C :=$ `chartAlgFin A K j` for the integral closure of $A[j]$ in $K$, and $X :=$ [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel A K j`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236) for the two-chart integral model, the pushout gluing $\operatorname{Spec}$ of $C$ and of the integral closure of $A[j^{-1}]$ along the middle chart, with structure map `toBase` to $\operatorname{Spec} A$ and open immersion `ιFin` from $\operatorname{Spec} C$. The ideal $y \subset C$ is maximal (`hy`), contains $\varpi$ (`hϖy`), and is supersingular in the sense of `hss`: for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi : C \to \Omega$ with kernel $y$, the value $\varphi(j)$ lies in [`ModularCurve.ssJSet q Ω`](def/ModularCurve_SupersingularModuli.html#L7), the set of elements $\xi$ such that every elliptic Weierstrass curve over $\Omega$ with $j$-invariant $\xi$ has no non-zero affine point killed by $q$. Here, for $\gamma \in SL_2(\mathbb{Z})$, a *level automorphism at $\gamma^{-1}$* means an $L$-algebra automorphism $\tau$ of $K$ with [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.IsLevelAutAt L q ζ q (q^2*M') H₁ γ⁻¹ K τ`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelLevelAutAt.html#L29): for every weight $k$, every pair of modular forms $f,g$ on $\Gamma_{H_1}(q^2M')$ of weight $k$ with integral $q$-expansions $p_f,p_g$, $p_g \neq 0$ as a series over $\mathbb{Q}$, and every $x \in K$ whose Laurent expansion is the coefficientwise image of $p_f/p_g$, the complex Laurent expansion of $\tau x$ (read through any $\iota$ with $\iota\zeta = e^{2\pi i/q}$) multiplied by the $q$-expansion of $g|_k\,$`conjElemN q γ⁻¹` equals the $q$-expansion of $f|_k\,$`conjElemN q γ⁻¹`.
--
--   The hypothesis `hArig` is a rigidity package at all supersingular points over $\varpi$: for every point $z$ of $X$ at which the germ of $\varpi$ lies in the maximal ideal of the stalk $\mathcal{O}_{X,z}$, every point $y'$ of $\operatorname{Spec} C$ with `ιFin` image $z$, and $y'$ supersingular in the sense of `hss` (clause `hss'`, stated for $y'.\mathrm{asIdeal}$), there exist a complete discrete valuation domain (written $W$ inside that hypothesis), a ring map $\sigma : A \to W$ with $\mathfrak{m}_W = (\sigma\varpi)$, power series $f,u,v \in W[\![X_0,X_1]\!]$ with $u,v$ units and $f \equiv X_0X_1^q - X_0^qX_1 \pmod{(X_0,X_1)^{q+2}}$ (the `drinfeldForm`), and a ring isomorphism $e$ from the adic completion of $\mathcal{O}_{X,z}$ onto $S := W[\![X_0,X_1]\!]/\bigl(C(\sigma(\varpi_t^{q+1}))\,v - f\,u\bigr)$, such that, writing `toC` for the completion map, `mkS` for the quotient map and `germY` for the composite $C \to \mathcal{O}_{X,z}$ through `ιFin`, the following seven clauses hold: (1) $e$ carries the germ of each $a \in A$ to the class of $C(\sigma a)$; (2) for $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$, every level automorphism at $\gamma^{-1}$ maps $C$ into $C$; (3) if moreover $\gamma_{11} \equiv 1 \pmod \ell$, then such a $\tau$ satisfies $\tau a - a \in y'$ for all $a \in C$; (4) for $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ and $\tau$ a level automorphism at $\gamma^{-1}$ preserving $C$ and fixing $y'$ modulo $y'$, there are a ring automorphism $\theta$ of $S$, an element $c \in W$ and a matrix $M \in M_2(W)$ with: $\theta$ intertwines, through $e \circ$ `toC` $\circ$ `germY`, the restriction of $\tau$ to $C$; $\theta$ fixes all constants $C(w)$; $\theta(X_j) \equiv \sum_i M_{ij}X_i$ modulo the square of the ideal generated by the classes of $X_0,X_1$; $c^{q+1} \equiv 1$ and $M_{ij} \equiv c\,\gamma_{ij}$ modulo $\mathfrak{m}_W$; $c \equiv 1$ modulo $\mathfrak{m}_W$ whenever $\gamma_{11}\equiv 1 \pmod\ell$; and $c \not\equiv 1$ modulo $\mathfrak{m}_W$ whenever $\gamma \in \Gamma(q)$ and $\tau \neq \mathrm{id}$; (5) branch separation: for integers $a_1,b_1,a_2,b_2$ and primes $P_1,P_2$ of $S$, each not containing both classes of $X_0$ and $X_1$, each containing the class of $C(\sigma\varpi)$ and an element of the form $a_iX_0 + b_iX_1 + h$ with $h \in (X_0,X_1)^2$, if $q \nmid a_1b_2 - a_2b_1$ then the contractions of $P_1$ and $P_2$ to $\mathcal{O}_{X,z}$ along $e\circ$ `toC` differ; (6) for a prime $P$ of $S$ as above whose tangent direction is $(1,0)$, an element $a \in C$ has germ in the contraction of $P$ if and only if every Laurent coefficient of $a$ lies in the image of $\mathfrak{m}_A$; (7) a Hasse-type clause: the series [`ModularCurve.jqNModC L q`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L18) lies in $K$ and in $C$, and there are $a_0 \in A$ with this element minus $a_0$ in $y'$, an integer $e_0 \ge 1$ and $h \in (X_0,X_1)^{e_0}$ such that for all $a,b \in W$ not both in $\mathfrak{m}_W$ with $a^qb - ab^q \in \mathfrak{m}_W$ the degree-$e_0$ leading form $\sum_{i\le e_0}\mathrm{coeff}_{(i,e_0-i)}(h)\,a^ib^{e_0-i}$ is a unit, and $e$ carries the germ of that difference to the class of $h$.
--
--   A particular such configuration is then fixed: a point $z$ of $X$ with germ of $\varpi$ in the maximal ideal of $\mathcal{O}_{X,z}$, a point $y'$ of $\operatorname{Spec} C$ over $z$ satisfying `hss'`, with $y'.\mathrm{asIdeal} = y$ (`hy'y`), together with a complete discrete valuation domain $W_1$, $\sigma_1 : A \to W_1$ with $\mathfrak{m}_{W_1} = (\sigma_1\varpi)$, series $f_1,u_1,v_1$ with $u_1,v_1$ units and $f_1$ congruent to the Drinfeld form modulo $(X_0,X_1)^{q+2}$, and an isomorphism $e_1$ from the adic completion of $\mathcal{O}_{X,z}$ onto $S_1 := W_1[\![X_0,X_1]\!]/(C(\sigma_1(\varpi_t^{q+1}))v_1 - f_1u_1)$; the hypothesis `hW₁` asserts for these data exactly the seven clauses (1)–(7) just described.
--
--   The ideal $J \subset C$ is, by `hJ`, the infimum of the set of ideals of the form $\tau^{-1}$ of the contraction, along $e_1 \circ$ `toC` $\circ$ `germY`, of the ideal of $S_1$ generated by the classes of $C(\sigma_1\varpi_t)$, $X_0$ and $X_1$, taken over all $\gamma \in \Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$ and all level automorphisms $\tau$ at $\gamma^{-1}$ preserving $C$. The $A$-subalgebra $B \subseteq K$ is, by `hB`, generated over $C$ by $\{x \in K : \exists\, i \in J,\ x\varpi_t = i\}$, the blow-up chart of $J$ in the coordinate $\varpi_t$. A valuation subring $W$ of $K$ is given with $B \subseteq W$ (`hBW`), subject to four further packages: `hR1` states that $C \le B$ and that every element of $K$ is a ratio of elements of $B$ with non-zero denominator; `hR2` states that $B$ is formally smooth and of finite presentation over $A$ and that $B/\varpi B$ has Krull dimension at most $1$; `hR3` (five clauses) states that $W \cap L$ is exactly the image of $A$, that $\mathfrak{m}_W$ is generated by $\varpi$, that $W$ is a discrete valuation ring, that for $b \in C$ one has $b \in y$ if and only if $b \in \mathfrak{m}_W$, and that $W$ is the localisation of $B$ outside $\mathfrak{m}_W$; `hEQ` (five clauses, summarised here) states that for every $\mathbb{F}_{q^2}$-algebra structure on the residue field $k$ of $A$ there is a surjection $\rho : B \to$ [`DrinfeldCurve.CoordRing q k`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L21) with kernel $\mathfrak{m}_W \cap B$, compatible with $A \to k$, and equivariant for level automorphisms $\tau$ at $\gamma^{-1}$ with $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ preserving $W$, through an element $c \in \mathbb{F}_{q^2}^\times$ with $(\,$`redQ q γ`$,c)$ in [`DrinfeldCurve.hSubgroup q`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L276) acting by `hAction`, with $c \neq 1$ when $\gamma \in \Gamma(q)$ and $\tau \neq \mathrm{id}$; that $B$ is stable under all level automorphisms for $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$; that every prime of $B$ containing $\varpi$ receives $\mathfrak{m}_W \cap B$ under some level automorphism with $\gamma \in \Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$; that an element of $B$ sent into $\mathfrak{m}_W$ by all such automorphisms is divisible by $\varpi$; and that a level automorphism preserving $y$ on $C$ preserves $W$.
--
--   Finally, `ends` is a finite set of subrings of $K$, characterised by `hends`: a subring $O$ belongs to `ends` if and only if there is a non-zero $a \in J$ such that, setting $B_a$ to be the $A$-subalgebra of $K$ generated over $C$ by $\{x \in K : \exists\, i \in J,\ x a = i\}$, there is a maximal ideal $P$ of $B_a$ with $O$ the localisation of $B_a$ at $P$ inside $K$, with every element of $y$ a non-unit of $O$ whenever it lies in $O$, and with $B \not\subseteq O$. The hypothesis `hperm` states that for $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ and every level automorphism $\tau$ at $\gamma^{-1}$ preserving $W$, each $O \in$ `ends` has an $O' \in$ `ends` with $f \in O \iff \tau f \in O'$.
--
--   The conclusion is a valuative covering statement: for every valuation subring $V$ of $K$ such that $V \cap L$ is exactly the image of $A$, such that $C \subseteq V$, and such that every element of $y$ lies in $\mathfrak{m}_V$, at least one of the following holds: either $B \subseteq V$; or there is an end $O \in$ `ends` such that $O \subseteq V$ and $V$ dominates $O$, that is, for every $f \in O$ one has $f \in V$, and if $f$ is not a unit of $O$ then $f \in \mathfrak{m}_V$.
--
--   This is the valuative-covering step for the blow-up of the supersingular chart at a point $y$ of the integral model of the modular curve of level $\Gamma_{H_1}(q^2M')$: every valuation ring of $K$ that is centred on $y$ and restricts to $A$ on $L$ either contains the blow-up chart $B$ or dominates one of the finitely many ends produced by the other charts of the blow-up. It is used in the assembly of the common chart, its stabiliser and the valuative cover for the same data, which packages the Drinfeld-chart rigidity input `hArig` into a single geometric conclusion.
